WEBVTT

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:11.150
<i>Ueno! Ueno!</i>

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.860
<i>We have just arrived at Ueno!</i>

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:18.890
<i>Please ensure that you retrieve all belongings before leaving the train!</i>

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.120
I hope you haven't forgotten anything, honey!

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.710
Hey, those country folk went out of their way to give this to us!

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:33.130
I ain't forgetting a thing!

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:36.630
Still, wasn't that a nice wedding?

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:41.540
You said it! And that bride was so cute!

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:44.640
She was so fair and thin...

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.580
You're saying that I'm dark and fat, aren't you?

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:50.650
Besides, we barely even had a decent ceremony ourselves!

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:54.130
But you were the one who wanted to elope!

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:59.600
And who was it that went crying and begging for that?

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:00.610
<i>Uh, excuse me.</i>

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:03.620
Sorry, but we need to take this car to the trainyard...

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:06.310
Oh, please forgive me.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:08.040
Sorry 'bout that.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:19.700
It's raining...

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:21.650
Never mind.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:25.370
I'm finally back...

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:28.100
in Tokyo, where Carlos awaits.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.060
Make it quick, honey!

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:39.320
H-Hey, isn't that Joe?

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:40.820
Joe?

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.880
You're right! It's Joe!

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:44.390
Joe!

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:44.390
<i>Joe!</i>

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.930
Joe!

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:45.930
<i>Joe!</i>

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:46.410
Joe!

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.650
And I thought we'd finally got a chance to meet Joe, but now he's gone.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:00.420
When did he get so mean?
He could at least give us a holler!

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.490
He was probably in a hurry.

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:05.430
Don't you worry! We'll see him again in the slums!

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:10.670
Besides, where else would that stray dog Joe go besides the slums?

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:12.380
You got a point there.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:30.060
Hey! Who's up for some day labor?

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.060
<i>Well, we're finally back.</i>

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:35.250
Hey, Gonta! You gonna work today or what?

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:39.990
Go on, honey. You just had two or three days off.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.030
Now get going!

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:48.010
I'm coming! I'm coming!

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:14.150
Hey! Danpei-san!

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:15.790
If it isn't Danpei-san!

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:20.290
You've done real good, I tell ya!

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:21.800
Done what?

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:24.280
Oh, you don't have to play dumb with me!

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.300
I know Joe's back!

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.580
Don't be ridiculous. Joe's not coming back.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:33.310
I saw him the other day, but he was as lively as a sleepwalker.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:37.520
Well that's odd... I guess he hasn't come to see you yet.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:40.860
What did you say? Are you trying to tease me?

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:44.320
N-No, I'm not! I saw Joe at Ueno Station this morning!

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.400
What?

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:49.700
I-It's true! The wife and I saw him!

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.870
Hey!

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.380
Stop the truck! Please!

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:02.880
My Joe's come back! Let me off!

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:09.300
Don't throw out your back!

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:09.300
<i>Say hi to him for us!</i>

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:16.000
That bastard made it back to Tokyo,

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.260
but I guess he was too shy to pay me a visit. That son of a...

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:21.980
Hang on...

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:25.760
Looking back, the touring manager told me

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:29.930
that he started spacing out ever since he saw that Carlos' match.

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:32.600
So the first place he'd go would be...

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:36.240
Oh, I get it now!

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:38.120
No wait...

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:42.200
But if he presses himself in his condition...

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:45.740
No, hang on...

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:48.320
What matters is that he's back in Tokyo!

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:25.540
Carlos has become so silent as of late, it's like he's a completely different person.

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:27.900
It's not the first time this has happened.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:31.550
I'd expect him to rave like a maniac, but he'd clam right up.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:37.490
And the more powerful his opponent is, the more silent Carlos gets.

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:42.560
He has perceived Joe Yabuki as his greatest opponent, and that makes him nervous.

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:57.680
Why don't you cheer Carlos up with a dance, my lady?

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:01.270
Whenever he gets this way, even I start getting melancholy.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:06.880
Carlos...

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:08.670
Carlos!

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:11.630
Quiet.

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:15.750
He is coming.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:20.770
Who's coming?

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:26.270
It's nothing. I must've imagined it.

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:42.370
You have a visitor, my lady.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:46.880
He claims to be your acquaintance, and he insists on seeing you.

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:50.990
He was wearing a shabby outfit and had a gleam in his eye.

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:53.490
He set me ill at ease so I tried to turn him away,

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:56.890
but he's sitting in the foyer and refuses to go home.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.410
What's his name?

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:01.230
I tried asking him, but he wouldn't tell me.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:03.200
I see. Then I'll come down and see for myself.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.710
You shouldn't go alone, my lady! It's too dangerous!

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:09.880
I'll be fine. I have two special bodyguards with me today.

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:17.910
I suppose he really has come.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.290
Yabuki-kun!

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:30.110
Hey!

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:45.330
This foyer is no place to talk.

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:47.020
Come upstairs.

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:49.050
No, this is just fine for me.

00:09:49.050 --> 00:09:51.590
I've collected a lot of dust over my tour.

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:54.030
Don't want to soil your pretty carpet.

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:57.780
So what do you want?

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:01.180
Well, you see...

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:02.560
To get right to the point...

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:05.500
I've come here to ask for employment.

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:07.580
Employment?

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:09.150
Yeah, employment.

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:11.900
I got thrown out of the troupe,

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:14.090
so I'm kind of unemployed now.

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:18.990
Have you lost your bite?

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:23.100
That is such a mundane request, it makes me want to cry!

00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:28.100
I take it that Carlos is here, right?

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:33.170
I stopped by Shiraki Gym on my way here,

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:35.470
but they sent me over here.

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:37.110
What would you do if he was?

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:39.720
From what I hear, now that he's beaten Nango,

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:41.270
he's scheduled to fight Harajima.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:46.580
And I figure he'll take on Tiger Ozaki after that.

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:49.580
What point are you trying to make?

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:54.900
If he had a sparring partner who's fought all three of them before,

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:57.590
I think that'd be a valuable asset to him.

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:03.600
And I'd like you to employ me as that sparring partner.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:09.250
Of course, "sparring partner" makes it sound real nice,

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:11.210
but really I'd just be a human sandbag.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:14.230
A foil, as they say in boxing terms.

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:18.470
That'd be just the right business for me.

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:22.200
Either way, I think this is in both our best interests.

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:24.730
Let's hire him!

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:31.620
Joe Yabuki, I could not ask for more!

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.380
No, Carlos!

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:34.880
C-Carlos!

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:36.690
Carlos Rivera...

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:38.880
Never thought you'd be the sensible type.

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:05.050
I take it we have a deal?

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:06.980
<i>All right</i>, Joe.

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:24.510
<i>Attention, members of the press!</i>

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:28.200
<i>We will now be exhibiting Carlos Rivera's sparring match!</i>

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:32.560
<i>All those who wish to report on this, please assemble by the ring in the practice arena!</i>

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:36.380
And to think that before his Nango match, he kept his dignity as a world ranked boxer

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:39.940
by not doing any public practices...

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:44.260
Why do you think he decided to hold a public sparring?

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:45.950
Either way, it'll at least make an article!

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:51.900
Hey, you see that?

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:52.790
That's Yabuki Joe!

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:56.900
Oh, so his sparring partner is Yabuki Joe!

00:12:56.900 --> 00:13:00.300
I heard he'd joined a touring troupe.

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:02.490
Guess he's now broke

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:07.290
and went to Shiraki Gym, the home of his former rival Rikiishi Toru, as a human punching bag.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:10.640
Almost makes me want to keep the camera off him!

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:12.520
Yabuki-kun, your gloves.

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:15.640
Here.

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:18.650
Why the hell are these gloves so huge?

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:21.800
Forget it! We're not baby-boxing or anything!

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:23.030
Come on, somebody explain this!

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:25.530
Those were my instructions.

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:29.520
I should've guessed you gave this pointless order!

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:31.140
These are sixteen-ounce gloves!

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:33.140
I'm not gonna ask for six-ounce match gloves,

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:35.540
but you could at least get me some ten-ounce gloves!

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:40.610
These gloves are more like overshoes than anything!

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:41.500
Well, why!?

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:47.130
Oh, right. I'm an employee.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:49.410
Guess I gotta follow the chairman's orders.

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:50.970
I got it, I got it.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:57.250
Hey, why don't we get going?

00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:59.980
I'm sure these reporters are getting impatient!

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:03.900
Hold it!

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:06.780
Put this sparring on hold!

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:09.350
Joe! You're really back?

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:10.930
What are you here for?

00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:11.880
Come on, Joe!

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:14.440
What's gotten into you,

00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:16.770
that's making you do this ridiculous sparring match?

00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:17.750
Ridiculous?

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:18.560
Yeah!

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:21.730
You can't do this sparring match! In fact, I outright forbid it!

00:14:21.730 --> 00:14:23.250
Now let's go back!

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.340
Hands off!

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:29.660
So the one time you show up after so long,

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:31.850
you decide to be the foolish one, old man?

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:32.970
Joe, wait!

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:34.350
Tange-san...

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:36.420
I understand your concern,

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:39.170
but they're each wearing sixteen-ounce gloves.

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:40.840
In kendo, this would be the equivalent

00:14:40.840 --> 00:14:43.380
of sparring in a dojo with bamboo swords.

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:45.100
There is nothing to concern you...

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:45.400
Oh...

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:48.220
Well, my apologies.

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:50.010
But even when sparring with bamboo swords,

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:53.910
a well-placed blow to the head could crack your skull open.

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:59.110
When I first heard Joe was back, I knew on instinct

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:04.380
that between these two was a bloodlust strong enough to crack their heads open!

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:07.200
I can't explain it,

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:09.880
it's a strong intuition based on my years of training fighters!

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:12.910
Tange-san, I absolutely agree with you!

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:16.910
Robert-san! I had a feeling you'd understand!

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:20.420
Come on, Robert-san! You have to do something to stop this sparring...

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:23.250
<i>Oh, yes!</i>  Let's cancel this!

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:26.050
My lady, as the owner of Shiraki Gym,

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:28.760
you have to prevent this sparring match!

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:39.660
Hey, what's so funny?

00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:43.880
There's something wrong with you all.

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:46.360
It's just a sparring match.

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:49.360
And besides, we're practically sparring with toy gloves.

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:53.330
And you're making a big deal about skulls and intuition?

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:54.390
Isn't that right, Carlos?

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:56.450
I can understand why Joe would laugh.

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:58.250
This is just sparring.

00:15:58.250 --> 00:15:59.330
I can guarantee that.

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:01.390
Now hurry and ring the bell!

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:02.770
Carlos!

00:16:10.510 --> 00:16:12.100
Come on, what's the matter?

00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:13.970
There's no need to be so formal!

00:16:15.770 --> 00:16:19.940
We don't need the bell to tell us when to spar.

00:16:22.060 --> 00:16:23.290
Ring the bell.

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:24.790
Please, wait!

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:26.040
Young lady!

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:27.560
Ring it now!

00:16:32.790 --> 00:16:38.790
Joe Yabuki, it's time I saw with my own eyes whether you're worthy of being my rival.

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:40.920
Way to go, Carlos.

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:42.630
Now we can go at it with all we got!

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:51.360
I'm starting to get the shivers from excitement!

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:52.530
What about you, Carlos-san?

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:54.950
Take that, you bastard!

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:05.150
You're a good one.

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:09.210
I don't see cheery fighters like you very often.

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:10.710
<i>Come on!</i>

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:29.460
Not bad, Carlos.

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:30.400
But just you watch!

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:03.890
Son of a bitch! He used the Cross Counter!

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:06.960
On top of that, he used the recoil off the ropes,

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:09.900
and hit his temple, right where he hit Rikiishi!

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:24.810
Did you see that punch?

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:26.480
Yeah. That oughta hurt.

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:27.980
Carlos looks weak in the knees!

00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:31.750
I guess Joe's still got a bit of the killer left in him!

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:35.260
That kinda gave me a jolt!

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.540
Joe Yabuki, I'm really happy.

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:42.160
My intuition served me right.

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:43.560
You truly are a formidable opponent.

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:46.790
So I'll just take you down, here and now!

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:48.560
That's how I do things!

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:50.750
Now I'm starting to feel his bloodlust!

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:52.830
He's like a black panther waiting to pounce on its prey!

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:55.590
Now you're fired up. So bring it, black panther!

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:16.800
Joe!

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:28.000
You finally got serious there.

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:30.670
Even if it was just for a second,

00:19:30.670 --> 00:19:33.050
that's what I wanted to see.

00:19:33.050 --> 00:19:37.340
I wanted to experience that physically, in the flesh!

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:39.070
Your real punch!

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:47.790
Say something, dammit!

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:00.800
No! Don't do it, Joe!

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:27.580
Stop it!

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:29.080
<i>No more, Carlos!</i>

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:30.580
Joe! Cut it out!

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:32.360
You can't go any further!

00:20:32.360 --> 00:20:33.580
Stop!

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:35.230
<i>No! No, Carlos!</i>

00:20:35.230 --> 00:20:36.080
<i>No!</i>

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:38.320
What the hell? And it was just getting good!

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:40.050
Come on, chairman, don't stop it!

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:48.910
Gentlemen, I apologize for stopping this partway,

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:52.000
but this will be the end of today's sparring match.

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:52.000
<i>You don't mean...</i>

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:54.500
Carlos, Yabuki-kun, get out of the ring.

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:57.060
It's an order from the chairman of Shiraki Gym.

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:04.390
Gentlemen, Carlos has his match against Harajima coming up,

00:21:04.390 --> 00:21:07.070
so we wouldn't want him ruining his form.

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:10.080
Well, when you put it that way, I can understand.

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:12.310
Still, what a real shame!

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:13.650
Carlos sure was sticking it to him.

00:21:13.650 --> 00:21:15.400
No, I'd say they were about even.

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:17.250
After all, Joe's punch took its toll on him.

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.240
So Joe the Wild Kid is back in action?

00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:21.250
This is getting interesting!

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:29.370
Carlos, we have to get to the showers!

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:30.760
I don't want you catching a cold.

00:21:45.180 --> 00:21:48.020
You better go get changed, too.

00:21:52.100 --> 00:21:53.080
Joe?

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:56.400
I'm fine. But his punches sure sting.

00:22:27.380 --> 00:22:29.350
What a fearsome foe Joe is...

00:22:29.350 --> 00:22:31.310
If we were fighting with six-ounce gloves,

00:22:31.310 --> 00:22:34.620
I'd be with Toru Rikiishi by now...

00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:43.130
Here's your payment as a sparring partner.

00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:44.740
I don't need your money.

00:22:44.740 --> 00:22:47.130
In fact, I'd rather be paying you for this.

00:22:47.130 --> 00:22:48.990
I figured you'd say that.

00:22:48.990 --> 00:22:51.890
That's why this envelope contains an invitation, and not money.

00:22:55.520 --> 00:22:57.920
Carlos Rivera vs. Harajima Ryu...

00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:04.520
I'm sure that you'll be able to see Carlos' tremendous power even better there.

00:23:19.150 --> 00:23:20.530
I'm looking forward to it.

00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:23.210
Tell Carlos I said that.

00:24:39.100 --> 00:24:42.020
Joe has finally returned to Namida Bridge,

00:24:42.020 --> 00:24:44.120
where he gets right to restoring Tange Gym.

00:24:45.110 --> 00:24:46.630
The children are overjoyed,

00:24:46.630 --> 00:24:49.170
and Noriko-chan works hard to help Joe out.

00:24:49.490 --> 00:24:53.530
But for whatever reason, Nishi is the only unhappy one.

00:24:53.530 --> 00:24:57.050
And Joe hears something he never expected to hear from Nishi.

00:24:58.270 --> 00:25:01.700
Now, as Joe and Nishi foster their manly friendship

00:25:01.700 --> 00:25:05.590
as they each set off down their own paths,

00:25:05.590 --> 00:25:07.630
which way is tomorrow!?
